# A lockfile is a resolution graph, not text: two graphs merged line by line can
# name versions no install ever resolved together. With `-merge`, when both
# sides of a merge changed it, git keeps the current branch's copy and reports
# a conflict instead. Resolution: docs/starter-as-upstream.md, "When both sides
# changed pnpm-lock.yaml". Diffs stay textual — this is not the `binary` macro.
pnpm-lock.yaml -merge
